Software For The Public Good &para;

The Apache&reg; Software Foundation (ASF) provides software for the public good, guided by community over code. Like the enduring oak tree, our projects thrive through the contributions of thousands worldwide.

Our Open Source Projects &para;

The ASF is the home of the world&rsquo;s most trusted open source projects in data, cloud, search, libraries, geospatial, IoT, and beyond.

Our Incubating Projects &para;

See All Incubating Projects

Incubate a Project &para;

Give your project a neutral, trusted home where communities flourish &mdash; with the ASF&rsquo;s expertise, tools, and support to help you succeed.

Everyone is Welcome &para;

At The ASF, contribution is for everyone. Whether code, docs, or ideas &mdash; your +1 makes a difference. Come contribute and grow with us.

New to The ASF? Start here

Upcoming Events &para;

Fluss Forward London &para;

September 22-23, 2026

Apache Fluss is open-source, lakehouse-native streaming storage that makes your data lakehouse truly real-time. Fluss Forward is where the community that builds and runs it comes together. This isn't a vendor showcase. It's a community event.

LakehLakehouse Day 2026 is an all-day, multi-track conference co-located with Community Over Code Glasgow 2026. Taking place on October 10, the event is dedicated to all things related to open lakehouse technologies under the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) umbrella, with content supporting Apache Iceberg&trade;, Apache Hudi, Apache Parquet&trade;, Apache Gravitino, Apache Polaris&trade;, and more.

Community Over Code Glasgow 2026 &para;

Glasgow, Scotland, UK &para;

Community Over Code Glasgow 2026 features four in-person days of sessions at the Hilton Glasgow for ASF members, committers, and open source developers from around the world, focusing on Search, Big Data, Internet of Things, Community, Geospatial, Financial Tech, and many other topics.

Community Over Code Sydney 2026 &para;

Sydney, Australia &para;

Community Over Code Sydney 2026 is a two-day intimate conference running two streams of diverse and interesting talks.

Thank You, Sponsors &para;

The ASF is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit, supported by individual and corporate donors who believe in secure software for the public good and the power of community over code.

Explore what&rsquo;s new at The ASF &mdash; from project news to community voices, all in one place.

